# DTF tier manifest: proxy-scan-db-update-grace  (artifact-keeper#6300)
# Profile-set: filesystem + the mock-scan-formats upstream (172.16.<slot>.72).
# Verdicts come from the backend image's bundled Grype and its pre-seeded DB:
# no scanner sidecar, no internet, so the tier can gate.
#
# WHAT IT GUARDS (#6300): a stored proxy verdict carries the scanner version it
# was graded with, and since #3287 that string includes the vulnerability-DB
# build (`grype-X.Y.Z+db-YYYY-MM-DD`). Every DB update therefore made every
# stored verdict stale at once, and the next pull of each cached package was
# scanned again on the request path under fail_closed (the client waited or got
# a 423) or queued a scan under fail_open, all in the same hour. Since
# 1.13.0, within a window of the fleet first seeing a new build, a verdict the
# same scanner binary graded against the PREVIOUS build decides the pull and
# the pull re-grades the bytes in the background. The window is 6 h by default
# for fail_open and record_only, and off by default for fail_closed
# (PROXY_SCAN_DB_GRACE_HOURS_FAIL_CLOSED is the operator's opt-in).
#
# The DB bump is simulated from the stored side: the previous build of the
# live binary is recorded as first seen a day ago, an older build is recorded
# a minute ago (a stale replica recorded late, which must NOT become the
# previous build), and the stored verdicts are rewritten to the previous build
# (log4j-core `clean`, as a build that did not know the advisory would have
# graded it).
#
# Phase 1, defaults:
#   CONTROL    a fail_closed pull is still re-scanned inline (opt-in only).
#   FIX #6300  fail_open pulls are decided by the stored verdicts
#              (X-AK-Scan: clean) with no scan on the request path. Pre-fix
#              (RED): served `pending`, a scan per pull.
#   CONTROL    both re-graded in the background; log4j-core then 403.
# Phase 2, the backend recreated with the fail_closed opt-in
# (fixtures/fail-closed-grace.yml):
#   FIX #6300  the clean jar's fail_closed pull is 200 with no scan on the
#              request path. Pre-fix (RED): re-scanned inline.
#   FIX #6300  the log4j-core pull is not blocked or scanned synchronously.
#              Pre-fix (RED): 403 after an inline re-scan.
#   CONTROL    both re-graded in the background; log4j-core then 403.
#   CONTROL    a verdict from another binary, and one from the stale build
#              recorded late, are re-scanned before the pull is answered.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-scan-formats"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
COVERS="6300"
